WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:02.968
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:03.834
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:04.834
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:05.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.701
Thank you for being here.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:08.834
[ Whistling ]

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.267
Well, guys,
I want to say congrats

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.300
to the Kansas Jayhawks,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.434
who won the NCAA Championship...

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.267
...after pulling off one
of the biggest --

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.434
the biggest, in fact,

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.868
the biggest comeback
in tournament history.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.267
Yeah, it was an amazing game.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:27.267
The Kansas players woke up today
like, "It felt like a dream.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.534
You were there
and you were there.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.701
The Tin Man, you were there."

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.834
Yeah, it was
the biggest comeback since the

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.334
"Can you hear me now?" guy got
that job working at Sprint.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.067
-Good gig.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.300
Speaking of comebacks, today,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.567
Tiger Woods, who's still
recovering from an injury

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.267
[ Whistling ]
that many thought
would end his career,

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.067
said that he plans to play
this week at the Masters.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.400
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:56.200
Golf announcers were so pumped,
they were like,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:56.934
[ Hushed ]
"This is amazing.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:01:00.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:04.567
I'm so friggin' excited
right now.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.033
I can barely contain myself.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.267
Just the tiniest amount of pee
just now."

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:13.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.133
-Oh.
-Yep, people thought Tiger
was done and, now, he's back.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.300
When he heard,
Tom Brady was like,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.067
"Uh, kind of my thing,
but whatevs. Okay."

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.200
Let's get to some news.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.567
Today former President Obama

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:25.934
returned to the White House

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.000
for the first time
since leaving office

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.934
and everyone there seemed
really happy to see him.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:30.934
Watch this.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.834
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:47.400
-Yeah. After a few minutes,
Biden was like,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.033
"Alright,
that's more than enough.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:53.033
Let's remember
who the vice president --

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:56.434
I mean, the president is.
I'm the president now."

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.434
Yep, Obama said
he would've visited sooner,

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.467
but gas prices
were too expensive.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:05.133
But it was fun to see the former
president at the White House.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.968
Obama felt like a guy who was
visiting his old high school

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.200
and Biden was like the old
gym teacher who never left.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.801
That's right, Obama returned
to the White House

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:16.601
and C-SPAN was all over
his big reunion with Biden.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.067
Check out the schedule.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.767
[ Classical music plays ]

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.167
[ Laughter and applause ]
-There you go. I love it.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.400
[ Cheering ]
Very down to the minute.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.100
Hey, get this -- I read that,
after taking on criticism

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.734
for their handling
of the pandemic,

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:57.133
the CDC has announced plans
to revamp the agency.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.868
[ Murmuring ]
Ooh. Yeah, this feels like

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.300
when Domino's ran those ads
that said,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.868
"We know we suck
and we're going to work on it."

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.834
[ Laughter ]
You remember that?

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.367
Yeah, the CDC was like,
"Step 1 to the revamp --

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.067
get Obama to come visit."

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.601
The CDC will announce
their plan next month

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.100
and then a new plan
the month after,

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.734
then go back
to the original plan.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.033
So far, their only idea is
to change their name

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.667
to the American Centers
for Disease Control,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.400
just as they can go by ACDC.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.868
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.334
Well, over the weekend,
thousands of flights

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.000
were delayed, due to bad weather

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.400
and flight attendants had
to get creative

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.701
to keep passengers entertained.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:39.834
This is real.
But watch this.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.734
-♪ If you're happy
and you know it ♪

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.267
♪ Clap your hands ♪
[ Clap-clap ]

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.300
♪ If you're happy
and you know it ♪

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.100
♪ Clap your hands ♪
[ Clap-clap ]

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.267
♪ If you're happy
and you know it ♪

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:52.133
♪ Then you really
oughta show it ♪

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.000
[ Cheering ]

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.601
-After a few minutes of that,
passengers were

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.267
begging the air marshal
to tase them.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.400
[ Laughter ]
They were, "Okay.
Let's just get it over.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.300
Let's get out of here."

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.467
And that wasn't the only plane
having fun during the delay.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.300
Take a look at what they did
to pass the time

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.234
on another flight.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.267
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:14.701
-[ Clapping ]
Hurry up!

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.734
-Toilet paper race.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.400
[ Laughter ]
-Toilet paper.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.968
A toilet paper race.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.968
It looks bad,
but on Frontier Airlines,

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.968
that's the hot towel
in first class, yeah, yeah.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.868
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
So, not bad.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:37.434
And, lastly, before we go, I'd
like to take a moment to thank

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.667
some of our sponsors
for tonight's show.

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:42.000
They don't always
fit in the commercial breaks,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.701
